# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ClaimWise — Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in values as needed.
# NEVER commit .env.local to Git. Server-side secrets must never
# be prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Supabase (required — auth, database and private storage) ──
# Both values are safe to be public: the URL + publishable key
# model replaces the legacy anon key. Row Level Security is the
# real enforcement layer. Do NOT add a service-role key here or
# to any NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable — it bypasses RLS entirely.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# ── Supabase Auth settings (configure in the dashboard, not here) ──
# Authentication → URL Configuration:
#   Site URL: your app URL
#   Redirect URLs: <app>/auth/callback
# Email confirmation: keep ON for production.
# Google OAuth: enable under Authentication → Providers → Google.
# No Google OAuth secret belongs in this file for that flow.

# ── Optional legacy integrations ──
# Used only by the legacy document-intelligence module, not the vault.
# GOOGLE_GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ── Optional: DigiLocker (official government document fetch) ──
# Apply for partner credentials at https://partners.digilocker.gov.in
# and register the redirect URI https://<your-domain>/api/digilocker/callback
# DIGILOCKER_CLIENT_ID=
# DIGILOCKER_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Optional overrides (defaults are usually correct):
# DIGILOCKER_REDIRECT_URI=
# DIGILOCKER_API_BASE=
# Optional long random string used to encrypt the short-lived token
# cookie. Falls back to the client secret when unset.
# DIGILOCKER_STATE_SECRET=

# ── Optional: public share links (/s/<token>) ──
# Anonymous viewers resolve links through the server, which needs the
# Supabase service-role key to validate a share and stream its bytes
# from the private documents bucket. Copy the "service_role" key from
# Supabase → Settings → API. Without it the share pages show an
# honest "not configured" message; everything else is unaffected.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ── Optional: OTP sensitive-action lock (SMS gateway) ──
# Opening stored vault documents re-verifies the OWNER's mobile with a
# one-time code. Codes are generated server-side, sha256-hashed at rest
# and rate limited. Choose ONE provider:
# Twilio (recommended):
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
# TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER=
# Or Msg91:
# MSG91_AUTH_KEY=
# MSG91_TEMPLATE_ID=
# Local testing without a provider: set OTP_DEV_BYPASS=1 — the code is
# then printed in the server console and shown in the UI. NEVER set
# this in production.
# OTP_DEV_BYPASS=
# Optional long random string used to encrypt the 5-minute elevation
# cookie (falls back to DIGILOCKER_STATE_SECRET):
# OTP_ELEVATION_SECRET=

# ── Public app metadata (safe to expose) ──
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_NAME=ClaimWise
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ── Optional E2E audit account ──
# Only used by e2e-audit.mjs. Create a reusable confirmed account
# through normal signup; the app never creates demo accounts.
# E2E_TEST_EMAIL=
# E2E_TEST_PASSWORD=
# E2E_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
